        "id": "scene_b2_u06_1",
        "desc": "A big round pink pig with a curly tail stands at the start of the stepping stones, which are far too little for its feet: one hoof on a stone, the stone wobbling. Hedgie measures the pig with a long reed; Bun shakes her head; Pip, trying to say the word, has said it backwards and looks at the pig cross-eyed; Beads sits on a lily pad. Beside the bank a shovel sticks out of a freshly dug hole with dirt flying. Hidden in the picture: the pig, the big pig next to a tiny mouse, the shovel digging. Grumble does NOT appear.",
